    ],
    "behavior": [
      "Stage 1 registers two half-width partial products of a*b and the valid flag; stage 2 combines them into the full 32-bit product.",
      "The final stage adds the registered product into the 32-bit accumulator when the piped valid is set.",
      "clear synchronously zeroes acc and valid_out, taking priority over accumulation.",
      "Latency from valid_in to valid_out is 3 cycles.",
      "32 accumulator bits = 24 product bits + 8 guard bits, enough for a 256-deep dot product with no overflow.",
      "Operands, product and accumulator are signed two's complement. The multiply must be a signed multiply and the product must be sign-extended into the accumulator.",
      "a carries 16-bit activations and b carries 8-bit weights, sign-extended to the 16-bit ports. The accumulator width depends on those ranges: a wider value on either port can overflow it."
